It bundles SolidJS (MIT), Chart.js (MIT, https://www.chartjs.org) and the IBM Plex
fonts (SIL Open Font Licence 1.1). Rust crates used by the engine and the shell are listed
in Cargo.lock; their licences are checked by `cargo deny check` (deny.toml).

The materials library (crates/core/data/materials.json) is built from Datum Atlas (MIT,
https://github.com/Edgar-Mendonca/Datum-Atlas) by tools/materials.py. Every value names its source;
those sources keep their own terms.

Water and steam properties (crates/core/src/fluids.rs) follow the IAPWS releases R7-97(2012) (IF97), R12-08
(viscosity), R15-11 (thermal conductivity) and R1-76(2014) (surface tension), published by the International
Association for the Properties of Water and Steam (http://www.iapws.org). Gas heat capacities use the NASA Glenn
7-coefficient polynomials (McBride, Zehe and Gordon, NASA/TP-2002-211556); gas viscosity
and conductivity are fits to the reference correlations named in docs/MEMORY.md.

